# Node ES-module scripts are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) they were checked out with
# CRLF, and Vitest could not load two of them (scripts/
# check-no-hardcoded-credentials.mjs, scripts/security-harness/run.mjs):
# importing them in a test failed with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected
# token", while the same files load fine with LF (as on Linux CI).
*.mjs text eol=lf
